<li><p class='igt' id='i346'><a href="//depts.washington.edu/dxmedia/Chapman/8__nox/mp3/347.mp3" class='audio'>hidden</a><span class='words' id='i346w'><span class="word" id="i346w0">&quot;Gila</span><span class="word" id="i346w1">dalik</span><span class="word" id="i346w2">ts'in'!</span><span class="word" id="i346w3">Xidonsiniɬtayh!"</span><span class="word" id="i346w4">yiɬne.</span></span><br /><span class='glosses' id='i346g'><span class="gloss" id="i346g0">come on</span><span class="gloss" id="i346g1">be quiet</span><span class="gloss" id="i346g2"></span><span class="gloss" id="i346g3">bring me in</span><span class="gloss" id="i346g4">he said</span></span><br /><span class='trans' id='i346ft'>&quot;'Be quiet! Let me in!" he said.'</span></p></li>
<li><p class='igt' id='i347'><a href="//depts.washington.edu/dxmedia/Chapman/8__nox/mp3/348.mp3" class='audio'>hidden</a><span class='words' id='i347w'><span class="word" id="i347w0">Daɬine'</span><span class="word" id="i347w1">tr'i'ne</span><span class="word" id="i347w2">&quot;viyan',"</span><span class="word" id="i347w3">yiɬne.</span></span><br /><span class='glosses' id='i347g'><span class="gloss" id="i347g0">but</span><span class="gloss" id="i347g1">it is said</span><span class="gloss" id="i347g2">no</span><span class="gloss" id="i347g3">she said</span></span><br /><span class='trans' id='i347ft'>'But she said &quot;no."'</span></p></li>
<li><p class='igt' id='i348'><a href="//depts.washington.edu/dxmedia/Chapman/8__nox/mp3/349.mp3" class='audio'>hidden</a><span class='words' id='i348w'><span class="word" id="i348w0">Yitots'in'</span><span class="word" id="i348w1">tr'i'ne</span><span class="word" id="i348w2">iɬt'e</span><span class="word" id="i348w3">tathtrax.</span></span><br /><span class='glosses' id='i348g'><span class="gloss" id="i348g0">then</span><span class="gloss" id="i348g1">it is said</span><span class="gloss" id="i348g2">continuousy</span><span class="gloss" id="i348g3">he started to cry</span></span><br /><span class='trans' id='i348ft'>'And he started to cry without ceasing.'</span></p></li>
<li><p class='igt' id='i349'><a href="//depts.washington.edu/dxmedia/Chapman/8__nox/mp3/350.mp3" class='audio'>hidden</a><span class='words' id='i349w'><span class="word" id="i349w0">Itrix</span><span class="word" id="i349w1">tr'i'ne</span><span class="word" id="i349w2">xidigaɬ</span><span class="word" id="i349w3">tthidinengath</span><span class="word" id="i349w4">tr'i'ne,</span><span class="word" id="i349w5">venhdida'</span><span class="word" id="i349w6">che</span><span class="word" id="i349w7">dranh</span><span class="word" id="i349w8">tr'i'ne.</span></span><br /><span class='glosses' id='i349g'><span class="gloss" id="i349g0">he's crying</span><span class="gloss" id="i349g1">it is said</span><span class="gloss" id="i349g2">finally</span><span class="gloss" id="i349g3">all night long</span><span class="gloss" id="i349g4">it is said</span><span class="gloss" id="i349g5">next day</span><span class="gloss" id="i349g6">also</span><span class="gloss" id="i349g7">day</span><span class="gloss" id="i349g8">it is said</span></span><br /><span class='trans' id='i349ft'>'While he cried, a night passed, and a day.'</span></p></li>
<li><p class='igt' id='i350'><a href="//depts.washington.edu/dxmedia/Chapman/8__nox/mp3/351.mp3" class='audio'>hidden</a><span class='words' id='i350w'><span class="word" id="i350w0">Xidigaɬ</span><span class="word" id="i350w1">tr'i'ne</span><span class="word" id="i350w2">viqa'</span><span class="word" id="i350w3">yadz</span><span class="word" id="i350w4">don'idiyoq</span><span class="word" id="i350w5">tr'i'ne.</span></span><br /><span class='glosses' id='i350g'><span class="gloss" id="i350g0">finally</span><span class="gloss" id="i350g1">it is said</span><span class="gloss" id="i350g2">his feet</span><span class="gloss" id="i350g3">loose</span><span class="gloss" id="i350g4">they became</span><span class="gloss" id="i350g5">it is said</span></span><br /><span class='trans' id='i350ft'>'Finally his feet became loose.'</span></p></li>
<li><p class='igt' id='i351'><a href="//depts.washington.edu/dxmedia/Chapman/8__nox/mp3/352.mp3" class='audio'>hidden</a><span class='words' id='i351w'><span class="word" id="i351w0">Ngiyiq</span><span class="word" id="i351w1">tthaɬyiq</span><span class="word" id="i351w2">xiyegheyo</span><span class="word" id="i351w3">tr'i'ne</span><span class="word" id="i351w4">chenh.</span></span><br /><span class='glosses' id='i351g'><span class="gloss" id="i351g0">below</span><span class="gloss" id="i351g1">kashim entry</span><span class="gloss" id="i351g2">he went in</span><span class="gloss" id="i351g3">it is said</span><span class="gloss" id="i351g4">again</span></span><br /><span class='trans' id='i351ft'>'He tried to go into the entryway again.'</span></p></li>
<li><p class='igt' id='i352'><a href="//depts.washington.edu/dxmedia/Chapman/8__nox/mp3/353.mp3" class='audio'>hidden</a><span class='words' id='i352w'><span class="word" id="i352w0">Yitots'in'</span><span class="word" id="i352w1">chenh</span><span class="word" id="i352w2">xanqadhitldziq</span><span class="word" id="i352w3">tr'i'ne.</span></span><br /><span class='glosses' id='i352g'><span class="gloss" id="i352g0">then</span><span class="gloss" id="i352g1">again</span><span class="gloss" id="i352g2">feet got stuck</span><span class="gloss" id="i352g3">it is said</span></span><br /><span class='trans' id='i352ft'>'And once again, his feet got stuck.'</span></p></li>
<li><p class='igt' id='i353'><a href="//depts.washington.edu/dxmedia/Chapman/8__nox/mp3/354.mp3" class='audio'>hidden</a><span class='words' id='i353w'><span class="word" id="i353w0">&quot;Gila',</span><span class="word" id="i353w1">xidonsiniɬtayh,"</span><span class="word" id="i353w2">yiɬne</span><span class="word" id="i353w3">tr'i'ne.</span></span><br /><span class='glosses' id='i353g'><span class="gloss" id="i353g0">come on</span><span class="gloss" id="i353g1">bring me in</span><span class="gloss" id="i353g2">he said</span><span class="gloss" id="i353g3">it is said</span></span><br /><span class='trans' id='i353ft'>&quot;'Please let me in," he said.'</span></p></li>
<li><p class='igt' id='i354'><a href="//depts.washington.edu/dxmedia/Chapman/8__nox/mp3/355.mp3" class='audio'>hidden</a><span class='words' id='i354w'><span class="word" id="i354w0">&quot;Daɬine'</span><span class="word" id="i354w1">xidongitidhatltalts'in',"</span><span class="word" id="i354w2">yiɬne</span><span class="word" id="i354w3">tr'i'ne.</span></span><br /><span class='glosses' id='i354g'><span class="gloss" id="i354g0">but</span><span class="gloss" id="i354g1">I will not let you in</span><span class="gloss" id="i354g2">she said</span><span class="gloss" id="i354g3">it is said</span></span><br /><span class='trans' id='i354ft'>&quot;'Oh no, I will not let you in," she said.'</span></p></li>
<li><p class='igt' id='i355'><a href="//depts.washington.edu/dxmedia/Chapman/8__nox/mp3/356.mp3" class='audio'>hidden</a><span class='words' id='i355w'><span class="word" id="i355w0">&quot;Dodo</span><span class="word" id="i355w1">ngitthing</span><span class="word" id="i355w2">nixitidheɬtthalts'i</span><span class="word" id="i355w3">xizro,"</span><span class="word" id="i355w4">yiɬne,</span><span class="word" id="i355w5">&quot;xidongitatltaɬ,"</span><span class="word" id="i355w6">yiɬne</span><span class="word" id="i355w7">tr'i'ne.</span></span><br /><span class='glosses' id='i355g'><span class="gloss" id="i355g0">no more</span><span class="gloss" id="i355g1">down</span><span class="gloss" id="i355g2">you do not see</span><span class="gloss" id="i355g3">plainly</span><span class="gloss" id="i355g4">she said</span><span class="gloss" id="i355g5">I will let you in</span><span class="gloss" id="i355g6">she said</span><span class="gloss" id="i355g7">it is said</span></span><br /><span class='trans' id='i355ft'>&quot;'If you never more look down (toward the river), I will let you in.'</span></p></li>
<li><p class='igt' id='i356'><a href="//depts.washington.edu/dxmedia/Chapman/8__nox/mp3/357.mp3" class='audio'>hidden</a><span class='words' id='i356w'><span class="word" id="i356w0">&quot;Ngonh</span><span class="word" id="i356w1">yiɬ</span><span class="word" id="i356w2">ngito'</span><span class="word" id="i356w3">yiɬ</span><span class="word" id="i356w4">dodo</span><span class="word" id="i356w5">xiviningiɬ'anh,"</span><span class="word" id="i356w6">yiɬne.</span></span><br /><span class='glosses' id='i356g'><span class="gloss" id="i356g0">your mother</span><span class="gloss" id="i356g1">and</span><span class="gloss" id="i356g2">your father</span><span class="gloss" id="i356g3">also</span><span class="gloss" id="i356g4">no more</span><span class="gloss" id="i356g5">you see them</span><span class="gloss" id="i356g6">she said</span></span><br /><span class='trans' id='i356ft'>&quot;'You will never see your mother and your father anymore.'</span></p></li>
<li><p class='igt' id='i357'><a href="//depts.washington.edu/dxmedia/Chapman/8__nox/mp3/358.mp3" class='audio'>hidden</a><span class='words' id='i357w'><span class="word" id="i357w0">&quot;Oghdixizro</span><span class="word" id="i357w1">xidongitatltaɬ,"</span><span class="word" id="i357w2">yiɬne.</span></span><br /><span class='glosses' id='i357g'><span class="gloss" id="i357g0">only</span><span class="gloss" id="i357g1">I'll let you in</span><span class="gloss" id="i357g2">she said</span></span><br /><span class='trans' id='i357ft'>&quot;'Only then will I let you in.'</span></p></li>
<li><p class='igt' id='i358'><a href="//depts.washington.edu/dxmedia/Chapman/8__nox/mp3/359.mp3" class='audio'>hidden</a><span class='words' id='i358w'><span class="word" id="i358w0">&quot;Ngo</span><span class="word" id="i358w1">getiy</span><span class="word" id="i358w2">soxo</span><span class="word" id="i358w3">gits'i</span><span class="word" id="i358w4">dingidiyoq,"</span><span class="word" id="i358w5">yiɬne</span><span class="word" id="i358w6">tr'i'ne.</span></span><br /><span class='glosses' id='i358g'><span class="gloss" id="i358g0">well</span><span class="gloss" id="i358g1">really</span><span class="gloss" id="i358g2">for me</span><span class="gloss" id="i358g3">badly</span><span class="gloss" id="i358g4">you have done</span><span class="gloss" id="i358g5">she said</span><span class="gloss" id="i358g6">it is said</span></span><br /><span class='trans' id='i358ft'>'You have done very badly by me.'</span></p></li>
<li><p class='igt' id='i359'><a href="//depts.washington.edu/dxmedia/Chapman/8__nox/mp3/360.mp3" class='audio'>hidden</a><span class='words' id='i359w'><span class="word" id="i359w0">&quot;Sigege'</span><span class="word" id="i359w1">nguxo'in</span><span class="word" id="i359w2">gitr'odighele',"</span><span class="word" id="i359w3">yiɬne.</span></span><br /><span class='glosses' id='i359g'><span class="gloss" id="i359g0">my child</span><span class="gloss" id="i359g1">because of you</span><span class="gloss" id="i359g2">he is unhappy</span><span class="gloss" id="i359g3">she said</span></span><br /><span class='trans' id='i359ft'>'Because of you, my child is unhappy.'</span></p></li>
<li><p class='igt' id='i360'><a href="//depts.washington.edu/dxmedia/Chapman/8__nox/mp3/361.mp3" class='audio'>hidden</a><span class='words' id='i360w'><span class="word" id="i360w0">&quot;Ngoxo</span><span class="word" id="i360w1">sidhuxdiy gidhik</span><span class="word" id="i360w2">ts'in'</span><span class="word" id="i360w3">duxo'in</span><span class="word" id="i360w4">xidongitatltaɬ,"</span><span class="word" id="i360w5">yiɬne.</span></span><br /><span class='glosses' id='i360g'><span class="gloss" id="i360g0">for you</span><span class="gloss" id="i360g1">I feel pity</span><span class="gloss" id="i360g2"></span><span class="gloss" id="i360g3">because of it</span><span class="gloss" id="i360g4">I will let you in</span><span class="gloss" id="i360g5">she said</span></span><br /><span class='trans' id='i360ft'>'But since I have pity on you, I will let you in."'</span></p></li>
<li><p class='igt' id='i361'><a href="//depts.washington.edu/dxmedia/Chapman/8__nox/mp3/362.mp3" class='audio'>hidden</a><span class='words' id='i361w'><span class="word" id="i361w0">Axaxiɬdik</span><span class="word" id="i361w1">xidonyiniɬtanh</span><span class="word" id="i361w2">tr'i'ne.</span></span><br /><span class='glosses' id='i361g'><span class="gloss" id="i361g0">then</span><span class="gloss" id="i361g1">she let him in</span><span class="gloss" id="i361g2">it is said</span></span><br /><span class='trans' id='i361ft'>'And then she let him in.'</span></p></li>
<li><p class='igt' id='i362'><a href="//depts.washington.edu/dxmedia/Chapman/8__nox/mp3/363.mp3" class='audio'>hidden</a><span class='words' id='i362w'><span class="word" id="i362w0">Axaxiɬdik</span><span class="word" id="i362w1">eyggit</span><span class="word" id="i362w2">du'ot</span><span class="word" id="i362w3">yughun'</span><span class="word" id="i362w4">xidon'idiyo</span><span class="word" id="i362w5">tr'i'ne.</span></span><br /><span class='glosses' id='i362g'><span class="gloss" id="i362g0">then</span><span class="gloss" id="i362g1">there</span><span class="gloss" id="i362g2">his wife</span><span class="gloss" id="i362g3">to her</span><span class="gloss" id="i362g4">he went in</span><span class="gloss" id="i362g5">it is said</span></span><br /><span class='trans' id='i362ft'>'He went inside to his wife.'</span></p></li>
<li><p class='igt' id='i363'><a href="//depts.washington.edu/dxmedia/Chapman/8__nox/mp3/364.mp3" class='audio'>hidden</a><span class='words' id='i363w'><span class="word" id="i363w0">Tr'edha</span><span class="word" id="i363w1">tr'i'ne</span><span class="word" id="i363w2">idedig</span><span class="word" id="i363w3">vinoghyiq</span><span class="word" id="i363w4">gathdlingh</span><span class="word" id="i363w5">tr'i'ne.</span></span><br /><span class='glosses' id='i363g'><span class="gloss" id="i363g0">behold</span><span class="gloss" id="i363g1">it is said</span><span class="gloss" id="i363g2">she too</span><span class="gloss" id="i363g3">below her eyes</span><span class="gloss" id="i363g4">something flowed</span><span class="gloss" id="i363g5">it is said</span></span><br /><span class='trans' id='i363ft'>'There she was, with her tears flowing.'</span></p></li>
<li><p class='igt' id='i364'><a href="//depts.washington.edu/dxmedia/Chapman/8__nox/mp3/365.mp3" class='audio'>hidden</a><span class='words' id='i364w'><span class="word" id="i364w0">Xiyiɬ</span><span class="word" id="i364w1">tr'i'ne</span><span class="word" id="i364w2">deɬne</span><span class="word" id="i364w3">yigginh</span><span class="word" id="i364w4">vu'ot,</span><span class="word" id="i364w5">&quot;gan</span><span class="word" id="i364w6">voqo</span><span class="word" id="i364w7">daɬts'idz</span><span class="word" id="i364w8">ntadiyoy?"</span><span class="word" id="i364w9">yiɬne</span><span class="word" id="i364w10">diqing'</span><span class="word" id="i364w11">anh.</span></span><br /><span class='glosses' id='i364g'><span class="gloss" id="i364g0">then</span><span class="gloss" id="i364g1">it is said</span><span class="gloss" id="i364g2">she said thus</span><span class="gloss" id="i364g3">that person</span><span class="gloss" id="i364g4">his wife</span><span class="gloss" id="i364g5">what</span><span class="gloss" id="i364g6">for it</span><span class="gloss" id="i364g7">this way</span><span class="gloss" id="i364g8">you came back</span><span class="gloss" id="i364g9">she said to</span><span class="gloss" id="i364g10">her husband</span><span class="gloss" id="i364g11">he</span></span><br /><span class='trans' id='i364ft'>'And she said to her husband, &quot;'why have you come back here?'</span></p></li>
<li><p class='igt' id='i365'><a href="//depts.washington.edu/dxmedia/Chapman/8__nox/mp3/366.mp3" class='audio'>hidden</a><span class='words' id='i365w'><span class="word" id="i365w0">Deɬne,</span><span class="word" id="i365w1">&quot;diva</span><span class="word" id="i365w2">nuq'oɬonh</span><span class="word" id="i365w3">vits'i</span><span class="word" id="i365w4">xidiningiyonh?</span></span><br /><span class='glosses' id='i365g'><span class="gloss" id="i365g0">she said thus</span><span class="gloss" id="i365g1">who</span><span class="gloss" id="i365g2">woman</span><span class="gloss" id="i365g3">to her</span><span class="gloss" id="i365g4">the one you went in</span></span><br /><span class='trans' id='i365ft'>&quot;'Who was that woman you went to?'</span></p></li>
<li><p class='igt' id='i366'><a href="//depts.washington.edu/dxmedia/Chapman/8__nox/mp3/367.mp3" class='audio'>hidden</a><span class='words' id='i366w'><span class="word" id="i366w0">Divasre'</span><span class="word" id="i366w1">anh</span><span class="word" id="i366w2">vughun'</span><span class="word" id="i366w3">dhedo</span><span class="word" id="i366w4">ts'i'at,"</span><span class="word" id="i366w5">yiɬne.</span></span><br /><span class='glosses' id='i366g'><span class="gloss" id="i366g0">I wonder</span><span class="gloss" id="i366g1">she</span><span class="gloss" id="i366g2">with her</span><span class="gloss" id="i366g3">you stay</span><span class="gloss" id="i366g4"></span><span class="gloss" id="i366g5">she said</span></span><br /><span class='trans' id='i366ft'>'I wonder if you mean to stay with her?"'</span></p></li>
<li><p class='igt' id='i367'><a href="//depts.washington.edu/dxmedia/Chapman/8__nox/mp3/368.mp3" class='audio'>hidden</a><span class='words' id='i367w'><span class="word" id="i367w0">Chel</span><span class="word" id="i367w1">che</span><span class="word" id="i367w2">di'ne</span><span class="word" id="i367w3">tr'i'ne,</span><span class="word" id="i367w4">&quot;Se</span><span class="word" id="i367w5">suxuyo' ghun'</span><span class="word" id="i367w6">gho</span><span class="word" id="i367w7">disiyoq</span><span class="word" id="i367w8">ts'ixi'a</span><span class="word" id="i367w9">disidene?"</span><span class="word" id="i367w10">yiɬne</span><span class="word" id="i367w11">tr'i'ne.</span></span><br /><span class='glosses' id='i367g'><span class="gloss" id="i367g0">young man</span><span class="gloss" id="i367g1">then</span><span class="gloss" id="i367g2">he said</span><span class="gloss" id="i367g3">it is said</span><span class="gloss" id="i367g4">I</span><span class="gloss" id="i367g5">of my own accord</span><span class="gloss" id="i367g6">from</span><span class="gloss" id="i367g7">I did</span><span class="gloss" id="i367g8"></span><span class="gloss" id="i367g9">you say so to me</span><span class="gloss" id="i367g10">he said</span><span class="gloss" id="i367g11">it is said</span></span><br /><span class='trans' id='i367ft'>'Then the man said, &quot;Did I do that of my own accord, that you should say that to me?"'</span></p></li>
<li><p class='igt' id='i368'><a href="//depts.washington.edu/dxmedia/Chapman/8__nox/mp3/369.mp3" class='audio'>hidden</a><span class='words' id='i368w'><span class="word" id="i368w0">Ts'an</span><span class="word" id="i368w1">axaxiɬdik</span><span class="word" id="i368w2">yit</span><span class="word" id="i368w3">xughun'</span><span class="word" id="i368w4">ntithido'</span><span class="word" id="i368w5">tr'i'ne.</span></span><br /><span class='glosses' id='i368g'><span class="gloss" id="i368g0">so</span><span class="gloss" id="i368g1">then</span><span class="gloss" id="i368g2">there</span><span class="gloss" id="i368g3">with them</span><span class="gloss" id="i368g4">he began to stay again</span><span class="gloss" id="i368g5">it is said</span></span><br /><span class='trans' id='i368ft'>'And then he began to live there with them again.'</span></p></li>
<li><p class='igt' id='i369'><a href="//depts.washington.edu/dxmedia/Chapman/8__nox/mp3/370.mp3" class='audio'>hidden</a><span class='words' id='i369w'><span class="word" id="i369w0">Axaxiɬdik</span><span class="word" id="i369w1">gits'i'in</span><span class="word" id="i369w2">ntedolts'in'</span><span class="word" id="i369w3">iɬt'et.</span></span><br /><span class='glosses' id='i369g'><span class="gloss" id="i369g0">then</span><span class="gloss" id="i369g1">elsewhere</span><span class="gloss" id="i369g2">he did not go</span><span class="gloss" id="i369g3">continuously</span></span><br /><span class='trans' id='i369ft'>'He never went anywhere else.'</span></p></li>
<li><p class='igt' id='i370'><a href="//depts.washington.edu/dxmedia/Chapman/8__nox/mp3/371.mp3" class='audio'>hidden</a><span class='words' id='i370w'><span class="word" id="i370w0">Yit</span><span class="word" id="i370w1">xiyan'</span><span class="word" id="i370w2">xitathdo'</span><span class="word" id="i370w3">tr'i'ne.</span></span><br /><span class='glosses' id='i370g'><span class="gloss" id="i370g0">there</span><span class="gloss" id="i370g1">only</span><span class="gloss" id="i370g2">they began to stay</span><span class="gloss" id="i370g3">it is said</span></span><br /><span class='trans' id='i370ft'>'He only stayed there.'</span></p></li>
<li><p class='igt' id='i371'><a href="//depts.washington.edu/dxmedia/Chapman/8__nox/mp3/372.mp3" class='audio'>hidden</a><span class='words' id='i371w'><span class="word" id="i371w0">Axaxiɬdik</span><span class="word" id="i371w1">yigginh</span><span class="word" id="i371w2">xivonh</span><span class="word" id="i371w3">diyix</span><span class="word" id="i371w4">sriɬti xine'onh</span><span class="word" id="i371w5">tr'i'ne.</span></span><br /><span class='glosses' id='i371g'><span class="gloss" id="i371g0">then</span><span class="gloss" id="i371g1">that person</span><span class="gloss" id="i371g2">their mother</span><span class="gloss" id="i371g3">her house</span><span class="gloss" id="i371g4">she hid</span><span class="gloss" id="i371g5">it is said</span></span><br /><span class='trans' id='i371ft'>'The mother concealed the house again.'</span></p></li>
<li><p class='igt' id='i372'><a href="//depts.washington.edu/dxmedia/Chapman/8__nox/mp3/373.mp3" class='audio'>hidden</a><span class='words' id='i372w'><span class="word" id="i372w0">Ts'an</span><span class="word" id="i372w1">axaxiɬdik</span><span class="word" id="i372w2">yigginh</span><span class="word" id="i372w3">chel</span><span class="word" id="i372w4">anh</span><span class="word" id="i372w5">dingonh</span><span class="word" id="i372w6">yiɬ</span><span class="word" id="i372w7">nixidinegts'in'</span><span class="word" id="i372w8">tr'i'ne.</span></span><br /><span class='glosses' id='i372g'><span class="gloss" id="i372g0">so</span><span class="gloss" id="i372g1">then</span><span class="gloss" id="i372g2">year after year</span><span class="gloss" id="i372g3">it is said</span><span class="gloss" id="i372g4">that person</span><span class="gloss" id="i372g5">young man</span><span class="gloss" id="i372g6">he</span><span class="gloss" id="i372g7">his own mother</span><span class="gloss" id="i372g8">with</span><span class="gloss" id="i372g9">he did not return</span><span class="gloss" id="i372g10">it is said</span></span><br /><span class='trans' id='i372ft'>'And year after year, that man never returned to his own mother.'<a href="#n38" class="notelink">38</a></span></p></li>
<li><p class='igt' id='i373'><a href="//depts.washington.edu/dxmedia/Chapman/8__nox/mp3/374.mp3" class='audio'>hidden</a><span class='words' id='i373w'><span class="word" id="i373w0">Ts'an</span><span class="word" id="i373w1">xidigaɬ</span><span class="word" id="i373w2">vinixeɬtsen'</span><span class="word" id="i373w3">tr'i'ne.</span></span><br /><span class='glosses' id='i373g'><span class="gloss" id="i373g0">so</span><span class="gloss" id="i373g1">finally</span><span class="gloss" id="i373g2">it is fenced off</span><span class="gloss" id="i373g3">it is said</span></span><br /><span class='trans' id='i373ft'>'And so the story is finished.'</span></p></li>
</ol></div><div id='notes'><h2>Notes</h2><ol><li><span class="footnote" id="n1">Chapman/Kari contained <em> azrine </em> (Kari)/<em> aˊrzunĭ </em> (Chapman), 'they say'. KH elected to leave this out.</span></li><li><span class="footnote" id="n2">Chapman has <em> allaˊ </em> 'well'. Kari's version of this word is <em> ala.</em></span></li><li><span class="footnote" id="n3">Chapman has <em> dûtĭçtaˊn </em> 'were brought'. Kari has <em> dititht'anh.</em></span></li><li><span class="footnote" id="n4">For a third person plural subject, <em> dixaght'an' </em> is expected.</span></li><li><span class="footnote" id="n5">sitting up on a platform</span></li><li><span class="footnote" id="n6">This and the next sentence are combined in Kari's version, but are separate in Chapman's.</span></li><li><span class="footnote" id="n7">Chapman's version has <em> qoyûˊxûhlvwûˊt </em> 'the curtain bellies out'. Kari transcribed this as <em> xuyixiɬvit (</em> 'it is caused to be concave').</span></li><li><span class="footnote" id="n8">Chapman: 'He turned it over in his mind.'</span></li><li><span class="footnote" id="n9">This is Chapman's translation. Kari has 'He thought I wonder where the people are.'</span></li><li><span class="footnote" id="n10">Chapman:  'Lo! they say, a sudden burst of light.' Chapman notes that <em> viyiɬ </em> could be either 'suddenly' or 'with him'.</span></li><li><span class="footnote" id="n11">Chapman has <em> Ăgûdeˊ </em> and Kari <em> agide.</em></span></li><li><span class="footnote" id="n12">Chapman translates <em> sŏˊqŏyoˊ (sixiyo') </em> as 'my wisdom (meditation)'. His free translation of this sentence is 'it is because of my intention that you came here.'</span></li><li><span class="footnote" id="n13">Chapman's version lacks <em> nedr.</em></span></li><li><span class="footnote" id="n14">Kari had <em> dinganh </em> 'backbone'. KH didn't know that word and substituted <em> gingin 'fish backbone'.</em></span></li><li><span class="footnote" id="n15">The Chapman/Kari version of this sentence is: <em> Axaxiɬdik che yitl'oyidighetrit tr'i'ne. </em> 'She gave him food again.' KH changed <em> che </em> 'again' to <em> chel </em> 'young man'.</span></li><li><span class="footnote" id="n16">This free translation is based on Chapman. Kari's translation of the sentence was:  'And then the man said, &quot;how long will I only stay in the house?&quot;'</span></li><li><span class="footnote" id="n17"><em> Xidhu'onh </em> normally means 'there is (3D object)'. Chapman translates <em> qai\dh ûon </em> 'is there?' and adds a footnote to that word:  'that is, he lost his sense to locality, his consciousness'.</span></li><li><span class="footnote" id="n18">This is based on Chapman's translation of <em> diyix </em> and free translation of the sentence.</span></li><li><span class="footnote" id="n19">Chapman has <em> wuhlähltûˊñ </em> '(but) I was asleep'. Kari has <em> viɬaɬtingh, </em> recorded here with KH. However, given the free translation of the sentence, a first person singular form would be expected, something like <em> viɬagitingh.</em></span></li><li><span class="footnote" id="n20">Chapman has <em> ahlaˊ </em> 'dear me' and <em> qûˊhltĭ </em> 'now'.</span></li><li><span class="footnote" id="n21">Kari has <em> ngiyixts'i </em> 'from inside', which KH recorded as <em> ngixits'i.</em></span></li><li><span class="footnote" id="n22"><em> one </em> is Holikachuk. (Deg Xinag is <em> on.)</em></span></li><li><span class="footnote" id="n23">Kari has <em> yandighelo </em> 'she undressed him'. Chapman has <em> yäntĭˊgellŏˊ' </em> 'she took off his parka'.</span></li><li><span class="footnote" id="n24">Kari has <em> dhagg </em> 'mouth, throat' instead of <em> dho.</em></span></li><li><span class="footnote" id="n25">Normally <em> xisrigidasd(d)het.</em></span></li><li><span class="footnote" id="n26">This free translation is based on Chapman. Kari had: &quot;there is nothing lacking here that you can get by working, so why say that?&quot;</span></li><li><span class="footnote" id="n27">Instead of <em> goqo dist'anhdi, </em> Chapman has <em> gâˊkâ ĭstăˊn qăĭ, </em> which he translates 'where I used to hunt'. He adds a footnote: 'that is, I had no luck'.</span></li><li><span class="footnote" id="n28">The first part of this sentence is not in Chapman.</span></li><li><span class="footnote" id="n29">Chapman's free translation:  &quot;How could I tell how the time passed, since I never went outside?&quot; Kari's free translation:  &quot;'How could I know that, since I never see outside?&quot;'</span></li><li><span class="footnote" id="n30">Chapman has <em> tĕnnĭˊqtû dran </em> 'four days'. Kari has <em> diniyhdi dranh.</em></span></li><li><span class="footnote" id="n31">Kari's <em> ixuda' </em> 'if'. Chapman has <em> aˊĭtdû'û </em> 'if thou shouldst (do that)'.</span></li><li><span class="footnote" id="n32"><em> ghela' ts'ixiyan' </em> 'is not at all' is an unusual negative construction. Chapman has <em>ûxaillûˊ' </em> 'she is not' <em> tsûqoyänˊ' </em> 'at all'.</span></li><li><span class="footnote" id="n33">Chapman had <em> ntdûqaiqûˊxudetoˊĭrsr </em> 'they tell what happened'. Kari's version was <em> nidixaghidet'osr.  </em> KH didn't really know this word.</span></li><li><span class="footnote" id="n34">KH unusually has <em> vi'ot </em> rather than <em> vu'ot </em> here.</span></li><li><span class="footnote" id="n35"><em> xoghli'eɬ </em> is expected for 'it's getting light'.</span></li><li><span class="footnote" id="n36">This was in the village he had lived with his wife, not his parents' village.</span></li><li><span class="footnote" id="n37">Chapman has <em> yädzûtoûniˊhl </em> 'will he get free'.</span></li><li><span class="footnote" id="n38">Kari has <em> gits'anxatitl'idaq </em> 'year after year' (<em> gits'anxatidldaq </em> expected) in this sentence, based on Chapman's <em> gĭtsanqŏˊqŏtĭhldyăˊk </em> 'year in and year out'.</span></li><li><span class="footnote" id="n39">Chapman's title was 'Story of a Young Man who was purified from Sin'. He noted it was told by 'Blind Andrew'. Kari's title was <em> Nox Idinihoninh Gixudhoy </em> 'The Blind Person's Story'. KH pluralized the title to <em> Nox Idinuhon \ldots</em></span></li></ol>
</div>
</div>
</body>
</html>

